    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="ro31">
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string" calcext:value-type="string">
      <text:p>string</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string" calcext:value-type="string">
      <text:p>map-0x3018-0xD6_0</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="2"/>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="ce2" office:value-type="string" calcext:value-type="string"><text:p>北の　おそれ山にいる　ミコに<text:span text:style-name="T1">\n</text:span></text:p><text:p><text:span text:style-name="T2">けっこん　できるか　占ってほしいわ</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string" calcext:value-type="string">
      <text:p>I should ask the priestesses of Mount Osore up north whether I&apos;ll ever find a husband...</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string" calcext:value-type="string">
      <text:p>ZenkiTN: I made this into &quot;husband&quot; and the next one into &quot;wife&quot; because this character is a lady and the next one is a man. Their line is basically the same, so the joke is that they&apos;re both asking for the same thing (to get married), not knowing that there is someone on the other side of the mountain having the same thought.</text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:formula="of:=IF([.F2450]=[.I2450]; &quot;UNTRANSLATED&quot;; &quot;&quot;)">
      <text:p/>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="1016"/>
    </table:table-row>
